POPULATING QUESTION AND ANSWER FIELDS WITH DATA -----------------------------------------------

How to populate each question and answer fields with data after the exam structure has been
created and number of questions specified, and create the final version of 
those questions and answers, and save them to the appropriate table, which the student will retrieve 
in the Brain Tester app (Tester) when beginning an exam. Each exam in this current version
is limited to ten (10) questions. 

WARNING!! Never type your questions and answers directly into the data fields. Always type Q&As into
a word processor or similar device,  then copy and paste that information into the appropriate fields. The Builder app 
is temperamental and all of your hard work may be lost. Also, database redundency is essential, and 
due to the significant amount of data involved, backing up everything on a separate hard drive will
greatly help prevent catastrophic loss and much work rebuilding the exams and questions. 

Fill in all fields to the extent possible, original questions and correct answers and detailed 
explanation if desired. Furthermore, REMEMBER to select one radio button to indicate which answer is 
the correct answer. The radio buttons as designed, for now, are grouped in such a way that only one 
answer can be selected. If nothing is selected all answers are considered false. 

Grading of the exam in the Tester is as follows. When creating a question and selecting the correct 
answer, that choice is set in an ArrayList of type Boolean. Currently five options are available. 
That Boolean list is stored in each question object (anonymous subclasses of QuestionSuper), (described subsequently). 
Initially all five Booleans are initialized to false. The correct answer is initialzed to true. 
The student in taking the exam ArrayList also makes a radiobutton selection into a similar list. 
When the question is evaluated it is those two lists that are compared for equality. If the lists 
are equal it is a pass, but if not, a fail, and initially or eventually the correct and incorrect answers are displayed. 

When ready, and the creator clicks the "Create Exam Question" button, the String data is assigned
to the 'questionArray' String array, and the prof's profsRadioButtonSelections list is created with the appropriate
selection. Both the String array and Boolean Arraylist, and ie. selectedExamIndex, previouslySelectedCommand,
are then forwarded to the QuestionFactory class via a call to the setQuestionArray() method. And after this call the
data is displayed in the textPanePreview section. 

