WHY NO UML CHART?  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This Swing app was built in Eclipse using WindowBuilder. The main class is BrainBuilder3.java, and 
roughly 3,000 lines of code are contained within the constructor. It's a one-way-street of sorts. Outside classes/objects can
be accessed from that constructor and used, but instances of those numerous classes cannot access, say, the textfields etc.,
within that BrainBuilder3 constructor. After all, how do you create an instance of that class from without while it is in the process of 
being constructed? It can't be done from what I can tell. Accordingly, a UML chart would consist of BrainBuilder3 at the top, 
with a spaghetti-string cluster of lines extending below connecting the many objects it utilizes, with interconnecting lines between the 
roughly 30 classes (not including the many anonymous QuestionSuper subclasses). But feel free to try. 

